t/shell.d/menu-test.sh; no compat finding records it","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P is in review.changes (modified, matchLevel function).","status":"confirmed"}},{"detail":"review.behaviorDiff ran 213 inputs over 5 partitions (corpus 17, data 176, lifecycle 14, scale 3, timing 3) with 0 differences. test/bdiff/harness.mjs drives JSONC parsing and the menu request lifecycle, and stubs rebuildDisplay with fixed rows (harness.mjs:252). Neither path calls searchScore with a query, so the result says nothing about ranking. I ran base 311d29c7 vs head d4b5ce10 rebuildDisplay under node vm with the shipped menu (scratch only). For vsc, base gives `setup.default.editor.vscode, install.editor.vscode, apps.code` and head gives `apps.code | ...`. For system, `system | apps.btop` becomes `apps.btop | system`. Root tu without apps is identical. These results are outside the package, so no behavior_changed claim can be typed.","refs":[{"id":"test/bdiff/harness.mjs","kind":"file","line":252},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711}],"severity":"medium","title":"Opinion (my own run, not engine-verified): the differential found no difference, but its harness does not exercise search ranking","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"rebuildDisplay pins every app row out of the drilldown rows before the menu rows (Menu.qml:702, 711). At the root every app is a drilldown row, and the default Apps submenu holds only apps. So no app competes with a menu row inside one sorted list. I put the bias back to -5 in the head MenuModel.js (scratch copy) and ran head rebuildDisplay for 544 queries (every letter, 234 two-letter queries, 12 words; at the root and