ine":711},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":377},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: should a keyword-only app match beat an exact-label menu entry?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Exact-label menu entry vs keyword-only app\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildDisplay"],"scenario":"root search 'tu' with one installed app matching: the divider between direct children (setup) and deeper entries (install.tui) is no longer drawn"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"For root `tu`, base gives `setup | install.tui ... apps.code ...` and head gives `apps.code | setup install.tui ...`. The current-menu rows and the deeper rows now share one section. The PR says only \"with the divider following them\". Our TKDP rewrite (\"one divider separates the apps from all menu entries\") and the witness at menumodel-replay.test.mjs:1406 codify the new form. That is our reading, not the author's statement.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":705},{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1406},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: is dropping the direct/deeper divider whenever an app matches intended?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Divider placement with direct, deeper and app matches all present\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildDisplay"],"scenario":"root search 'e' with 200 installed apps: index of the first menu row in the result list"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"Every matching app now precedes every menu row. In my own scratch run at d4b5ce10 with synthetic apps that all match `e`, the first menu row moved from index 0 (base 311d29c7) to index 20 with 20 apps and to index 200 with 200 apps. The PR screenshots show one-app cases only.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: with many installed apps, do short queries bury every menu entry?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Burial at scale\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js:searchScore"],"scenario":"property: for every tier value and kind, max app score*1000+depth*25+order < min menu/link score*1000"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The invariant \"exceeds every match tier\" exists only in a comment. A future tier at 98 or above would let a menu row outrank an app wherever both share a sorted list: a non-app entry an extension adds to Apps, or a direct searchScore caller. The root display would not change, because the pinning orders it. The MC/DC replay pins today's values, not the invariant.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":377},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: does the -100 bias stay above every tier if a tier >= 98 is added? (opinion: name the constant)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Tier-gap invariant property test\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"testResults: ingested, current, 59 passed / 0 failed / 0 skipped (8 tagged tests, all joined). The rise from 57 is the baseline's two emoji picker tests, not this PR. test/shell.d/menu-compositor-test.sh and menu-acceptance-test.sh appear in review.tests with outcome passed. Of the 73 obligation cells in claimEvidence, 39 are observed_pass and 34 are not_linked, meaning no test is tagged with that class. The not_linked cells are not tested evidence. SJ7P (4 passed) and TKDP (3 passed) are observed_pass as changed as intended.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-compositor-test.sh","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-acceptance-test.sh","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-3JG5","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-4079","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-50RE","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-8CQ4","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-B757","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-NM45","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-Z48F","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"Obligation cells: 39 observed_pass, 34 not_linked; the live-session menu tests have observed outcomes","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"review.effects is absent for this JS/QML change. The empty spec-gap list therefore proves nothing about uncodified connections (see the review.scope approximations). From reading the code: searchScore's only callers are the Menu.qml searchScore() wrapper (line 559), which feeds rebuildDisplay, plus test assertions. resolveRoute does not use it. These are facts from reading, not engine-verified facts.","refs":[{"id":"review.effects.approximations","kind":"check"},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":559}],"severity":"info","title":"Change effects were not analyzed (effects_unavailable); uncodified connections cannot be detected","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:5798ebb94b9a93396a154c4d1d9d1dd49e11d86b41e8d23b09dab0abe1e00a70","packageIdentity":"epkg-5b2cbd87e9b889ae7ed8902db72f3fb6138b8a99664254eb99be5b6608751c90","riskAssessment":{"level":"medium","rationale":"The change deliberately reorders every menu search. Enter's target changes for many queries, including some where a menu entry matches the label exactly. It carries 4 unapproved compatibility changes, plus an inverted upstream assertion that no compat finding records. The configured differential does not exercise ranking. The engine rates risk low on gates and coverage. This assessment is advisory only."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":12,"rationale":"Pins the maintainer's decision either way. Root 'system' with btop installed, and 'terminal' with Alacritty: assert which row is first in rebuildDisplay's output.","refs":[{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1425}],"title":"Exact-label menu entry vs keyword-only app"},{"forClaim":13,"rationale":"For root 'tu' with one matching app, assert the boundary count and position. This turns the divider change into a decided, pinned behaviour.","refs":[{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1406}],"title":"Divider placement with direct, deeper and app matches all present"},{"forClaim":14,"rationale":"With 200 synthetic app rows, record the index of the first menu row for one-letter queries and assert a bound the maintainer accepts.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711}],"title":"Burial at scale"},{"forClaim":15,"rationale":"Enumerate tiers x kinds x realistic depth/order and assert app max < menu min. It fails loudly if a tier >= 98 is added. Add one case with a non-app entry inside Apps, where the bias decides the order.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":377}],"title":"Tier-gap invariant property test"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** Upstream #12223 (ax1g) ranks installed apps above menu entries in menu search. On the mirror it is commit d01bdd1e, identical to upstream head b74292ac. `searchScore` changes the app bias from -5 to -100 (MenuModel.js:377). `rebuildDisplay` pins matching app rows above the current menu's rows and re-derives the divider (Menu.qml:699-713). Upstream also adds a `vsc` test to menu-test.sh and inverts one assertion. Every later mirror commit is our proof work: spec text and witnesses, the #10340 test, citation re-points, two reviews, a KI note and trace re-reviews.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** The changed decisions are covered: 0 uncovered lines or outcomes. The run ingested 59 results: 59 passed, 0 failed. I re-ran the node suites at d4b5ce10: 30 passed, 1 skip (#10601 needs Qt). Base 311d29c7 vs head `rebuildDisplay`: for `vsc` VS Code now comes first; for `system` btop sits above the exact-label System menu. In my runs the display order comes from the pinning alone: with the bias put back to -5, 544 queries gave the same rows.\n\n**Compatibility.** The 4 compat findings are unapproved, each a compat_change_unapproved disclosure that prevents ready. Two are test_diff changes and two are removed-behaviour items in the #10340 test helper. All four follow the PR's stated intent. The 32 auditor notes shown with the package are notes, not approvals; only a human reviewer approves. The differential ran 213 inputs with no difference, but its harness does not exercise ranking.\n\n**Questions for a human.** (1) Should a keyword-only app beat an exact-label menu entry? (2) Is dropping the direct/deeper divider when an app matches intended? (3) Can many apps bury menu entries? (4) Should the bias stay, given the pinning already decides the order?\n\n**Traceability.** SJ7P and TKDP were modified; 39 more are code_changed through file-level traces. The PR does not touch shell/services/AppSearch.js (SW-REQ-261003-C9GM) or the emoji picker's search (SW-REQ-261004-JATY). No spec-gap candidates; effects were not analyzed.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** No check failed; 13 were skipped by configuration. The two extra test results (emojis-test.sh, menu-emoji-picker-test.sh) come from the baseline. Readiness is not_assessed. The next decision is human_judgement (compat_changes_unapproved), by a reviewer."}
